{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"GHSA-4q5r-gwcx-24m9","published":"2026-07-20T12:33:09Z","modified":"2026-09-04T20:30:04.265306393Z","withdrawn":"2026-09-04T20:12:37Z","summary":"Duplicate Advisory: SurrealDB: Graph traversal bypasses table SELECT permissions","details":"## Duplicate Advisory\n\nThis advisory has been withdrawn because it is a duplicate of GHSA-vjjx-rfw4-rmfc. This link is maintained to preserve external references.\n\n## Original Description\nSurrealDB versions before 3.1.0 fail to enforce table SELECT permissions when traversing graph edges or back-references. Authenticated users can read records from any table reachable through graph edges regardless of the target table's PERMISSIONS FOR select clause.","affected":[{"package":{"name":"surrealdb","ecosystem":"crates.io","purl":"pkg:cargo/surrealdb"},"ranges":[{"type":"SEMVER","events":[{"introduced":"0"}]}],"database_specific":{"last_known_affected_version_range":"< 3.1.0","source":"https://github.com/github/advisory-database/blob/main/advisories/github-reviewed/2026/07/GHSA-4q5r-gwcx-24m9/GHSA-4q5r-gwcx-24m9.json"}}],"references":[{"type":"WEB","url":"https://github.com/surrealdb/surrealdb/security/advisories/GHSA-vjjx-rfw4-rmfc"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-63746"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/surrealdb-before-permission-bypass-via-graph-traversal"}],"database_specific":{"cwe_ids":["CWE-200"],"github_reviewed":true,"github_reviewed_at":"2026-09-04T20:12:37Z","nvd_published_at":"2026-07-20T12:19:44Z","severity":"HIGH"},"severity":[{"type":"CVSS_V3","score":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N"},{"type":"CVSS_V4","score":"CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N/E:X/CR:X/IR:X/AR:X/MAV:X/MAC:X/MAT:X/MPR:X/MUI:X/MVC:X/MVI:X/MVA:X/MSC:X/MSI:X/MSA:X/S:X/AU:X/R:X/V:X/RE:X/U:X"}]}